aid","primary":true},{"source":"04 Debt/Cinderbrook Bank loan statement September 2026.pdf","locator":"PDF page 1; the bank’s loan statement for June 30 to September 30, 2026, with the interest debited each month","sha256":"1c13492894922ecf096323d2f3c9795f27cafa5c3b6cb266602cf2a5d7bf7874","name":"E07 Loan Statement","originalSheet":null,"kind":"loan","primary":true},{"source":"01 Client Accounting/June 30 2026 contract schedule.xlsx","locator":"Jun 30 2026!A8:O14; each job’s contract, estimate and cost at June 30, 2026","sha256":"4c1dba21add7d2049dde1c9273f571a10052a3f7376cd956ca150ea56c5e459c","name":"E03 Job Schedule","originalSheet":"Jun 30 2026","kind":"wip","primary":true},{"source":"01 Client Accounting/June 30 2026 contract schedule.xlsx","locator":"Jun 30 2026!A8:O14; each job’s contract, estimate and cost at June 30, 2026","sha256":"4c1dba21add7d2049dde1c9273f571a10052a3f7376cd956ca150ea56c5e459c","name":"E03 Completed Fy2026","originalSheet":"Completed FY2026","kind":"wip","primary":false},{"source":"01 Client Accounting/June 30 2026 contract schedule.xlsx","locator":"Jun 30 2026!A8:O14; each job’s contract, estimate and cost at June 30, 2026","sha256":"4c1dba21add7d2049dde1c9273f571a10052a3f7376cd956ca150ea56c5e459c","name":"E03 Jun 30 2025","originalSheet":"Jun 30 2025","kind":"wip","primary":false}],"openItems":[{"id":"UL-01","status":"open","amount":"186400.00","explanation":"Sound Ridge Mechanical’s pay application 7 (SRM-2604-07) is for HVAC work in place on Pier 9 from June 1 to 30, 2026, certified July 3, received July 9, 2026 and booked in July; it was paid on August 8. Proposed: debit job cost $186,400.00, credit accounts payable $177,080.00 and retainage payable $9,320.00. The machine never posts."},{"id":"UL-02","status":"open","amount":"23480.00","explanation":"Pellham & Quist LLP’s invoice 2026-0712 of July 12, 2026, $23,480.00, is for legal work from May 4 to June 30, 2026: the Corliss lien and the subcontract form review. It was unpaid at October 15 and nothing was accrued. Proposed: debit general and administrative expense, credit accrued liabilities."},{"id":"UL-03","status":"open","amount":"9440.00","explanation":"The utilities accrual of $6,200.00 was May’s yard and office bill and left out temporary site power. June’s bills were $15,640.00. Proposed: debit job and office costs, credit accrued liabilities, $9,440.00. Under clearly trivial alone; listed because it repeats each month."},{"id":"UL-04","status":"open","amount":"28665.00","explanation":"June’s interest, $17,040.00 on the term loan and $11,625.00 on the line, was debited by the bank on July 1 and recorded in July. Accrued interest at June 30 is nil. Proposed: debit interest expense, credit 2410 accrued interest, $28,665.00. The quarterly review found the same practice (interest recorded when paid)."},{"id":"CROSS-01","status":"open","amount":"204835.16","explanation":"UL-01 adds $186,400.00 to Pier 9 Lofts’ cost at June 30. Revenue is cost-to-cost, so the same correction would add $204,835.16 of revenue and reduce the overbilling: a net $18,435.16 increase in income. The CPA settles it together with the job schedule testing’s CO-07 finding before posting either."},{"id":"MAT-01","status":"open","amount":"340000.00","explanation":"Materiality is proposed at $340,000.00, 0.5% of the year’s revenue, with performance materiality $255,000.00 and clearly trivial $17,000.00. The engagement partner sets the final amounts."},{"id":"REP-01","status":"open","amount":null,"explanation":"No management representation letter has been obtained. It should state that all liabilities, including those for work done before June 30 and billed later, are recorded."},{"id":"SIGN-01","status":"open","amount":null,"explanation":"These are draft workpapers and a draft findings memo for the engagement partner. They are not an audit report and give no opinion. Nothing has been signed, posted or sent."}],"incomplete":true,"research":null,"filing":"audit-liab-hgc","returnFile":"Liabilities Findings DRAFT.pdf","returnLabel":"Draft Findings Memo for the CPA","periodLabel":"June 30, 2026"}